Part B — Hands-on Lab 1: Public & Private IPs (quick)
Goal
See how PIPs and private IPs behave, and how NSGs control access.
Steps
1.	Resource Group
•	Create rg-ip-lab in your preferred region.
2.	VNet + Subnet
•	VNet: vnet-ip-lab = 10.20.0.0/16
•	Subnet: snet-app = 10.20.1.0/24
3.	Windows VM
•	VM: vm-web-01 (Windows Server 2019/2022) in snet-app.
•	Public IP: enable (Static).
•	NSG inbound:
o	Allow RDP 3389 from Your IP
o	Allow HTTP 80 from Internet (optional if you install IIS)
4.	Validate
•	RDP to PIP → works because NSG allows it.
•	(Optional) Install IIS and browse http://<public IP>.
 

5.	Switch to private-only (just to see the difference)
•	Disassociate the VM’s public IP (or disable).
•	Try RDP again from your PC → fails (no Internet path).
 

•	Keep this VM; you’ll reach it later via VPN Gateway.
